// One-off import: every eD system a.s. (edshop.edsystem.cz) graphics card whose chip is
// NVIDIA GeForce RTX 40-series or higher (RTX 4060 through RTX 5090 — the "40xx series and
// higher" scope Jakub asked for), across every board-partner brand eD stocks for those chips.
// AMD/Intel cards and anything RTX 30-series or older are skipped (out of the requested scope);
// professional/workstation lines (RTX PRO, RTX xxxx Ada, RTX A-series, Quadro) are excluded too
// since they aren't part of the RTX 40/50 consumer chip lineup this import targets.
//
// Like scripts/import-gpu-variants.mjs (the earlier buildcores-sourced GPU-variant import), eD
// system is B2B with prices hidden behind login, so there's no real per-SKU price to scrape. But
// unlike that script, this catalog already has 6 real manufacturer-variant rows curated for every
// one of these 15 chipsets, and — critically — every existing variant of a given chipset already
// shares the exact same flat price/tier/passmark regardless of brand (confirmed by querying the
// live catalog: all 6 existing "RTX 4090" variants are priced at 1599, all 6 "RTX 4060" variants
// at 299, etc.). So each new SKU here is priced by looking up its chipset in CHIPSET_TABLE below
// (built from that already-established per-chipset convention, using the MEDIAN of the existing
// rows for that chipset so a one-off outlier like the curated "RTX 5090 FE" — priced far above
// every AIB "RTX 5090" partner card — doesn't skew the number new rows get).
//
// RTX 5050 is deliberately excluded: eD stocks it, but the catalog has no existing "RTX 5050"
// row at all to derive a price/tier from, and inventing a brand-new price estimate (rather than
// reusing an established one) is exactly the kind of live-catalog guess that should be confirmed
// with Jakub first rather than silently applied — flagged in the run's summary output instead.
//
// Images follow the same convention as scripts/import-edsystem-motherboards.mjs and
// scripts/import-edsystem-cpus.mjs: the bare "_0a.jpg" master image downloaded and re-hosted in
// the component-images Supabase Storage bucket, not hotlinked.
import { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js';

